# Single-File Sequential Deployment Pipeline

## What Changes

Replace the current 3 separate workflow files with **one unified pipeline file** where:
- Phases run **sequentially** (enforced by `needs:`)
- A **human approval gate** sits between each phase (enforced by GitHub Environment)
- One `workflow_dispatch` button starts the entire flow

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The following files will be **deleted**:
> - `pre-deploy.yml`
> - `post-deploy.yml`
> - `deploy.yml`
>
> They are replaced by a single new file: `deploy-pipeline.yml`

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **GitHub Environment setup required (one-time):**
> For the approval gates to work, go to:
> `GitHub → Your Repo → Settings → Environments → production`
> → Enable **Required Reviewers** and add yourself (or your team).
> Without this, the gates won't pause — jobs will auto-proceed.

---

## How the Pipeline Flows

```
You click "Run workflow" (one button)
        │
        ▼
┌─────────────────────────┐
│   JOB 1: pre-deploy     │  Runs automatically
│   Black, isort, Flake8  │
│   MyPy, Bandit, pytest  │
└──────────┬──────────────┘
           │ passes
           ▼
    ⏸ GitHub pauses
    "Waiting for review"     ← You click Approve in GitHub UI
           │
           ▼
┌─────────────────────────┐
│   JOB 2: deploy         │  environment: production
│   Runs deploy command   │  (approval gate enforced here)
└──────────┬──────────────┘
           │ passes
           ▼
    ⏸ GitHub pauses
    "Waiting for review"     ← You click Approve in GitHub UI
           │
           ▼
┌─────────────────────────┐
│   JOB 3: post-deploy    │  environment: production
│   Smoke / health tests  │  (approval gate enforced here)
└─────────────────────────┘
```

